---
description: Preserve error causes, model expected failures explicitly, and never log sensitive business data.
globs: **/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: true
---

# Errors and logging

- Treat every caught value as `unknown` and normalize it before reading Error properties.
- Preserve the original failure with `cause` when wrapping an unexpected error.
- Do not catch only to rethrow unchanged, swallow failures, or convert every failure into a generic message.
- Model expected validation and business failures as typed results when the UI must render them.
- Keep domain errors independent of HTTP and Next.js.
- Translate infrastructure failures at the adapter/application boundary without exposing database details.
- Prefer one rich operational event per operation over scattered logs.
- Never log client names, contact details, free-text notes, receipts, tokens, secrets, raw bodies, or unnecessary financial data.
- Do not use incidental `console.log` in application code or record the same error at every layer.
